From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:07:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 070/105] arm64: dts: exynos7570: j4lte: leave eMMC HS400 off
 for now

HS400 passes the read and write tests, but large package installs on the
HS400 system corrupt data in ways not yet explained. Run at HS200 until the
cause is known; the HS400 timing properties stay in the node.

Signed-off-by: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7c326f27dcb571210139f110d686df5ca73351b7)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
index a49c7e1ad..b59a8044b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7570-j4lte.dts
@@ -140,7 +140,12 @@ &mmc0 {
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
-	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+	/*
+	 * HS400 works (see the ULP timing above) but is left off until the data
+	 * corruption seen during large package installs is explained. It is
+	 * suspected, not proven, to be involved.
+	 */
+	/* mmc-hs400-1_8v; */
 	no-sd;
 	no-sdio;
 
